    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Indie, platform jumping, ultra-short RPG. Come and uncover the mystery behind the protagonist's background together!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >[Game Features]</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Simple and intuitive controls</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Exciting and thrilling gameplay</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A story full of mysteries</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A black home page, monochromatic grass, monochromatic characters, text-based tutorials laid out directly, drifting characters, a character that automatically looks to the right, areas almost entirely represented by text alone, a castle you can enter without any guidance, a monochromatic interior of the castle, a second level where you don\u2019t know where to go, lights that don\u2019t change between morning and night, a health bar that isn\u2019t centered, a young hero in the story who shouldn\u2019t be able to fly but does, a chase scene with no sense of urgency, misaligned dialogue boxes, characters that haven\u2019t changed in twenty years\u2026</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >[Development Team]</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Developer: Budai</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Art (TBD): Jeannie Cheung</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Music: Sara Garrard</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Indie, platform jumping, ultra-short RPG. Come and uncover the mystery behind the protagonist's background together!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >[Game Features]</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Simple and intuitive controls</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Exciting and thrilling gameplay</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A story full of mysteries</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A black home page, monochromatic grass, monochromatic characters, text-based tutorials laid out directly, drifting characters, a character that automatically looks to the right, areas almost entirely represented by text alone, a castle you can enter without any guidance, a monochromatic interior of the castle, a second level where you don\u2019t know where to go, lights that don\u2019t change between morning and night, a health bar that isn\u2019t centered, a young hero in the story who shouldn\u2019t be able to fly but does, a chase scene with no sense of urgency, misaligned dialogue boxes, characters that haven\u2019t changed in twenty years\u2026</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >[Development Team]</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Developer: Budai</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Art (TBD): Jeannie Cheung</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Music: Sara Garrard</p>",
